# Call and answer: an event score for one person and one resident, on the synth and
# the TR-808. About a minute at 120 bpm.
#
# The machine keeps time, shows each instruction and listens. Only "do" lines make it
# act, from a short fixed list. The instructions are open: the players decide what
# "answer" means. A resident reads the instruction now, the next one and the phrase to
# answer with exec_command name=event_score action=state, and what sounded with name=hear.

title Call and answer
tempo 120
part person the person at the console
part wib a resident

1 all     listen: the drum machine counts you in
do tr808 preset electro
do tr808 tempo 120
do tr808 play
do synth patch bass
4 person  play a phrase on the synth, four to eight notes
4 wib     answer the last phrase
2 all     rest two bars
4 wib     play a phrase of your own, lower
4 person  answer the last phrase
do synth voice pcspk
4 all     play together on the PC speaker until someone repeats a note
do synth voice fm
2 all     rest, and let the drums finish
do tr808 stop
